Hi there!
I took a look at the Demo, and as far as I could understand, the "problem" is on the calculations of the method .distancePerFrame that is on the Game_Character( or Game_CharacterBase). This method plays a crucial role on the screen scrolling/camera when the player is moving.
It seems to me that this method is not, let's say, compatible, with a character speed that is not an integer (like 3.5 speed for example).
The default player speed is 4, if the diagonal speed of the player is 75% of it's normal speed, it will be 3.something.
Tested with Galv and also my Diagonal plugin. Although, my diagonal plugin does not work with %, but with a number to represent the speed. So, I could always put the diagonal speed = Player Speed - 1.
So Whatever speed I changed for the player, the jitter did not happen. The problem is, that -1 to the player speed when moving diagonally is too much, and the movement on diagonal stays much slower than the regular direction movement.
Understood that, I believe, we would need to find a calculation for the distance per frame that would be friendly with decimal numbers.
Or set the diagonal speed to be the same as the regular movement speed or -1.
( I also did try a lot of other things, like rounding the calculations number like someone said above. Update the characters positions, parallax position and map display positions all together, but none of that seems to solve the issue).
