Wow, thanks for all this testing!
I feel that the question remains: if the RM works like this and looks jittery, how on earth did Galv get his parallax sprites to scroll so differently? It seems like he must have his own entire process for updating the position that can handle decimals better, otherwise you'd see the same kind of jitter on his sprites. On maps with no events and just his parallax map, everything looks as it should when moving diagonal.
I don't know much about code, but the RM almost looks to me like it is "stepping" up then left by 1 px per frame each, whereas Galv's sprites are skipping the "up" and then moving "up+left" all at once, so it looks diagonal.
